    title: "Herzog warns Netanyahu of 'highly explosive and dangerous reality' amid rising settler violence",
    summary: "Herzog warns Netanyahu of 'highly explosive and dangerous reality' amid rising settler violence Israeli President Isaac Herzog warned Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu other senior officials of a \"highly explosive and dangerous reality\" in the West Bank amid increasing settler violence. \"The IDF commanders, the police officers and the Shin Bet personnel present a worrying picture of limited tools and a shortage of manpower,\" Herzog wrote in the letter sent to Netanyahu, Defence Minister Israel Katz, the Israeli army chief of staff Eyal Zamir and Attorney General Gali Baharav-Miara. Herzog said that the elections in Israel, the US and the Palestinian Authority - the latter has since been postponed - alongside the olive harvest season are set to \"create a highly explosive and dangerous reality\". \"A severe flare-up on the ground is liable to carry severe and far-reaching consequences, both for Israel’s security and its functioning as a sovereign state, and for Israel’s international standing, Diaspora Jewry, the Israeli economy, and more,\" the Israeli president further warned. He added that there is a \"moral disgrace and the stain on us\" when innocent Palestinians are harmed, and stressed that \"there is no room for this lawlessness in a sovereign state\".",
    preview: "Herzog warns Netanyahu of 'highly explosive and dangerous reality' amid rising settler violence Israeli President Isaac Herzog warned Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu other senior officials of a \"highly explosive and dangerous reality\" in the West Bank amid increasing settler violence. \"The IDF commanders, the police officers and the Shin Bet personnel present a worrying picture of limited tools and a shortage of manpower,\" Herzog wrote in the letter sent to Netanyahu, Defence Minister Israel Katz, the Israeli army chief of staff Eyal Zamir and…",
    body: "Herzog warns Netanyahu of 'highly explosive and dangerous reality' amid rising settler violence Israeli President Isaac Herzog warned Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu other senior officials of a \"highly explosive and dangerous reality\" in the West Bank amid increasing settler violence. \"The IDF commanders, the police officers and the Shin Bet personnel present a worrying picture of limited tools and a shortage of manpower,\" Herzog wrote in the letter sent to Netanyahu, Defence Minister Israel Katz, the Israeli army chief of staff Eyal Zamir and Attorney General Gali Baharav-Miara.\n\nHerzog said that the elections in Israel, the US and the Palestinian Authority - the latter has since been postponed - alongside the olive harvest season are set to \"create a highly explosive and dangerous reality\". \"A severe flare-up on the ground is liable to carry severe and far-reaching consequences, both for Israel’s security and its functioning as a sovereign state, and for Israel’s international standing, Diaspora Jewry, the Israeli economy, and more,\" the Israeli president further warned.\n\nHe added that there is a \"moral disgrace and the stain on us\" when innocent Palestinians are harmed, and stressed that \"there is no room for this lawlessness in a sovereign state\".",
